<h2>Chapter 2: Optimizing Every GBP Field</h2>
<h3>Business Description: Your 750-Character Sales Pitch</h3>
<p>Your business description is the only place in your GBP where you can write a free-form narrative about your company. You have 750 characters — use every single one.</p>
<p>Google does not use your description as a direct ranking factor. But it does influence click-through rate, and it feeds into AI-generated answers in Google Maps and AI Overviews. A well-written description pre-qualifies leads before they ever call you.</p>
<p><strong>Structure your description in this order:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Lead with primary service + location</strong> (first 150 characters visible in some contexts)</li>
<li><strong>List your top 3-4 specific services</strong></li>
<li><strong>Include trust signals:</strong> years in business, licenses, certifications, insurance</li>
<li><strong>Add differentiators:</strong> 24/7 availability, free estimates, same-day service, warranty</li>
<li><strong>End with service area mention + call to action</strong></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Example — Roofing Contractor:</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>"ABC Roofing is a full-service roofing contractor serving the greater Houston area since 2008. We specialize in roof replacement, roof repair, storm damage restoration, and new construction roofing for residential homeowners. Licensed, insured, and GAF Master Elite certified. Free inspections and estimates. Serving Houston, Katy, Sugar Land, The Woodlands, and Pearland. Call today to schedule your no-obligation roof assessment."</p>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>Example — Plumber:</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>"Licensed and insured plumbing contractor serving Dallas and the DFW Metroplex since 2015. We specialize in emergency plumbing, sewer line repair, water heater installation, and residential repiping. Available 24/7 for emergencies. Family-owned, 5-star rated, and committed to fair pricing with no hidden fees. Serving Dallas, Plano, Frisco, McKinney, and Garland. Call today for a free estimate."</p>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>What to avoid:</strong><br />
- Keyword stuffing ("best plumber emergency plumber cheap plumber Dallas")<br />
- All caps or excessive punctuation<br />
- URLs or HTML (they will not render)<br />
- Promotional language that sounds like an ad ("unbeatable prices!!!")</p>
<h3>Service Attributes</h3>
<p>Google allows you to select attributes that describe your business. These appear as icons and labels on your profile and help customers filter search results.</p>
<p><strong>Critical attributes for home service businesses:</strong></p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Attribute</th>
<th>Why It Matters</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Online appointments</strong></td>
<td>Customers can book directly from your profile</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Onsite services</strong></td>
<td>Confirms you come to the customer's location</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Free estimates</strong></td>
<td>Removes friction for price-sensitive shoppers</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>24/7 availability</strong></td>
<td>Critical for emergency trades (plumbing, HVAC, electrical)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Credit cards accepted</strong></td>
<td>Standard expectation; missing it raises questions</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Veteran-owned / Women-owned</strong></td>
<td>Differentiators that appear in search filters</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Licensed / Insured</strong></td>
<td>Trust signals that reduce customer anxiety</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Check your attributes monthly. Google adds new options regularly, and missing a relevant attribute means you will not appear when customers filter by it.</p>
<h3>Business Hours</h3>
<p>Set accurate hours and update them for holidays. According to a 2025 BrightLocal study, 38% of consumers check business hours on Google Maps before deciding to contact a business. Incorrect hours lead to missed calls and negative reviews.</p>
<p><strong>For 24/7 emergency services:</strong> List your regular office hours (for example, 7:00 AM – 6:00 PM) and add "Open 24 hours" as a special hours note, or clarify in your description that emergency service is available after hours.</p>
<p><strong>Special hours:</strong> Update holiday hours at least two weeks in advance. Google sends notifications to customers when your hours change, and accurate holiday hours prevent frustrated customers from leaving negative reviews.</p>
<h3>Phone Number Strategy</h3>
<p>Use a local phone number, not a toll-free number or personal cell phone. Local numbers signal geographic relevance to Google and build trust with customers who expect a local contractor.</p>
<p><strong>Best practices:</strong><br />
- Use a dedicated business line (Google Voice, CallRail, or a local carrier)<br />
- Keep your GBP phone number identical to the number on your website, Yelp, and all directories<br />
- If you use call tracking, implement dynamic number insertion on your website so the number shown matches your GBP number for consistency<br />
- Answer calls during listed business hours. Google's data shows that businesses answering calls within three rings convert 40% more leads than those that go to voicemail</p>
<h3>Website Link</h3>
<p>Link your GBP to a dedicated local landing page, not your generic homepage. If you serve multiple cities, create a location-specific page for each primary service area and link to the one that matches your verification address.</p>
<p><strong>Example URL structure:</strong></p>
<pre><code>Homepage: https://www.mikesplumbing.com/
Dallas page: https://www.mikesplumbing.com/plumber-dallas/
Plano page: https://www.mikesplumbing.com/plumber-plano/
</code></pre>
<p>Link your GBP to the Dallas page if your verification address is in Dallas.</p>
<p>Add UTM parameters to your GBP website link so you can track traffic in Google Analytics:</p>
<pre><code>https://www.mikesplumbing.com/plumber-dallas/?utm_source=google&amp;utm_medium=organic&amp;utm_campaign=gbp
</code></pre>
<h3>Appointment Link</h3>
<p>If you use online scheduling (ServiceTitan, Housecall Pro, Calendly, Acuity), add your booking link to the appointment URL field. This creates a direct conversion path from your profile to a scheduled job.</p>
<h3>Products and Services</h3>
<p>The Services section is separate from your description and is indexed by Google for search relevance. Add every individual service you offer, not just broad categories.</p>
<p><strong>Example for a plumber:</strong></p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Service</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Emergency Plumbing</td>
<td>24/7 emergency pipe repair, burst pipe fixes, and water shut-off assistance</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Drain Cleaning</td>
<td>Professional drain cleaning that eliminates clogs, prevents backups, and restores water flow</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Water Heater Installation</td>
<td>Tank and tankless water heater installation with same-day service available</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Sewer Line Repair</td>
<td>Trenchless sewer repair, camera inspections, and line replacement</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Toilet Repair</td>
<td>Leak fixes, running toilet repair, and new toilet installation</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Faucet Installation</td>
<td>Kitchen and bathroom faucet repair and replacement</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Residential Repiping</td>
<td>Whole-home copper and PEX repiping with lifetime warranties</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Include starting prices when possible (for example, "Drain Cleaning — Starting at $99"). Price transparency pre-qualifies leads and reduces price-shopping calls that waste your time.</p>
