<h2>Chapter 4: GBP Posts That Generate Leads</h2>
<h3>Post Types and When to Use Them</h3>
<p>Google Business Profile offers four post types. Each serves a different purpose in your lead generation strategy:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Post Type</th>
<th>Best For</th>
<th>Frequency</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Update</strong></td>
<td>General announcements, tips, completed projects</td>
<td>1-2x per week</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Offer</strong></td>
<td>Discounts, seasonal specials, limited-time deals</td>
<td>1x per week</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Event</strong></td>
<td>Open houses, community events, seasonal prep workshops</td>
<td>As needed</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Product</strong></td>
<td>Specific services with pricing</td>
<td>1x per week</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>Update posts:</strong> Share completed project photos with a brief description. "Just finished a full roof replacement in the Oak Lawn neighborhood. This home went from damaged shingles to a GAF Timberline HDZ system with a 50-year warranty. Swipe to see the transformation."</p>
<p><strong>Offer posts:</strong> These now display with bold "Limited Time Offer" tags directly below your contact information. They are the most visible post type. "Spring AC Tune-Up Special — $89 through May 31. Includes full system inspection, filter replacement, and refrigerant level check. Book online or call today."</p>
<p><strong>Event posts:</strong> Use these for community engagement. "Free Home Energy Audit Workshop — Saturday, June 14 at 10 AM. Learn how to lower your summer cooling bills by up to 30%. RSVP at [link]."</p>
<p><strong>Product posts:</strong> List specific services with starting prices. "Whole-House Repiping — Starting at $3,500. PEX or copper options available. Lifetime warranty included. Free estimate."</p>
<h3>Post Content Templates by Trade</h3>
<p><strong>HVAC Contractor:</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>"Is your AC blowing warm air? Before you panic, check these 3 things: 1) Is your thermostat set to COOL? 2) Is your outdoor unit free of debris? 3) Is your air filter clean? If you have checked all three and still have issues, call us for same-day service. Serving [City] and surrounding areas since [Year]."</p>
</blockquote>
