<h2>Chapter 5: Review Generation and Management</h2>
<h3>Why Reviews Are Your Ranking Engine</h3>
<p>Reviews are the second-most important ranking factor for local pack visibility, behind only your primary category. But it is not just about total count. Three metrics matter:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Total number of reviews</strong> — signals longevity and volume of business</li>
<li><strong>Average star rating</strong> — 4.7+ stars is the threshold for top-3 placement</li>
<li><strong>Review velocity</strong> — the consistent flow of new reviews over time</li>
</ol>
<p>A 2025 Semrush analysis found that businesses ranking in the top three positions of the local pack averaged 561 reviews with a 4.8-star rating. More critically, 73% of consumers consider reviews older than three months to be irrelevant. A profile with 200 reviews but none in the last six months will be outranked by a competitor with 80 reviews and 5 new ones this month.</p>
<h3>Review Generation Scripts</h3>
<p>The best time to ask for a review is immediately after job completion, when customer satisfaction is at its peak. Train your technicians to ask in person, then follow up with a text or email.</p>
<p><strong>In-person script (technician to customer):</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>"[Customer name], I am glad we could get this [service] taken care of for you today. Your feedback really helps our small business. Would you mind taking two minutes to leave us a quick review on Google? I can send you the link by text right now."</p>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>Text message follow-up (sent within 2 hours):</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>"Hi [Name], thanks for choosing [Company] for your [service] today. Your feedback helps other homeowners find trusted contractors. Would you take 2 minutes to share your experience? [Direct review link] Thank you! — [Technician name]"</p>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>Email follow-up (sent 24 hours later for non-responders):</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>"Subject: How did we do? Quick feedback request</p>
<p>Hi [Name],</p>
<p>Thanks again for letting us handle your [service] yesterday. We hope everything is working perfectly.</p>
<p>If you have a moment, would you share your experience on Google? It takes about 2 minutes and means the world to a small local business like ours.</p>
<p>[Review link]</p>
<p>Thanks for supporting local,<br />
[Owner name], [Company]"</p>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>Pro tip for keyword-rich reviews:</strong> After receiving verbal praise, say: "I am so glad to hear that. When you leave your review, if you could mention that we did the [specific service] in [neighborhood/city], that would be incredibly helpful for other homeowners searching for [service] in the area."</p>
<p>This plants a seed without being manipulative. Customers who had a great experience are happy to include specifics.</p>
