<li>Scores 7-8: Internal feedback form for improvement</li>
<li>Scores 1-6: Alert manager for immediate follow-up</li>
</ol>
<p>This filters unhappy customers away from public reviews while directing satisfied customers to your GBP.</p>
<h3>Responding to All Reviews</h3>
<p>Respond to every review — positive and negative — within 24-48 hours. Your responses perform for two audiences: the reviewer and every future customer reading your profile.</p>
<p><strong>Positive review response template:</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>"Thank you so much, [Name]! We are thrilled that your [specific service] turned out exactly as you hoped. It was a pleasure working on your [project type] in [neighborhood]. If you ever need [related service], we are just a call away. — [Owner/Manager name]"</p>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>Negative review response framework:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Acknowledge:</strong> Thank them for the feedback</li>
<li><strong>Apologize:</strong> Express genuine regret for their experience</li>
<li><strong>Explain briefly:</strong> Provide context without being defensive</li>
<li><strong>Take it offline:</strong> Provide a direct phone number or email</li>
<li><strong>Invite back:</strong> Show you want to make it right</li>
</ol>
<blockquote>
<p>"[Name], we are truly sorry your experience did not meet the standard we hold ourselves to. We take your concerns seriously and would like to make this right. Please call me directly at [phone] or email [email] so we can discuss what happened and find a solution. — [Owner name], Owner"</p>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>Never:</strong> Argue with the reviewer, disclose private details, or use copy-pasted generic responses. Future customers judge your character by how you handle criticism.</p>
<h3>Review Velocity Strategy</h3>
<p>Aim for 8-15 new reviews per month. Sporadic bursts (20 reviews one month, zero the next) look unnatural and may trigger Google's spam filters. A steady, consistent flow signals a healthy, active business.</p>
