<h2>Chapter 7: GBP Insights and Analytics</h2>
<h3>Understanding GBP Performance Data</h3>
<p>Google Business Profile Insights (now called "Performance" in the updated 2025 interface) shows how customers find and interact with your profile. Access it by searching for your business name on Google while logged into your management account, then clicking "Performance."</p>
<p>Google only retains six months of search query data, so export your data monthly to maintain historical records.</p>
<h3>Search Queries Report</h3>
<p>The search queries report shows the exact terms users typed before your profile appeared. This is keyword research gold — it tells you what real customers in your area are searching for.</p>
<p><strong>How to use the data:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>
<p><strong>Identify keyword opportunities:</strong> Look for queries you appear for but have not optimized. If "emergency plumber 2am" appears frequently and you offer 24/7 service, feature that prominently in your description and posts.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Track monthly trends:</strong> Export data monthly to spot seasonal patterns. "AC repair" searches spike in May-July. "Furnace repair" spikes in October-December.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Calculate engagement efficiency:</strong> Divide customer actions (calls, website clicks, direction requests) by total profile views. A low ratio means your profile needs better photos, descriptions, or reviews.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h3>Photo Views</h3>
<p>Photo views indicate how engaging your visual content is. Compare your photo views to your total profile views. If your profile gets 1,000 views but your photos only get 200 views, your cover photo is not compelling enough to click.</p>
<p><strong>Benchmark:</strong> Optimized contractor profiles average 735 photo views per 1,260 total profile views (58% photo engagement rate).</p>
<h3>Direction Requests</h3>
<p>Direction requests are less relevant for SABs since customers do not visit your location. However, a high number of direction requests combined with low call volume may indicate that customers think you have a storefront. Check that your address is hidden and your service-area status is clear.</p>
<h3>Call Tracking</h3>
<p>Track calls from your GBP by using a dedicated phone number or call tracking software. Compare GBP call volume to calls from other sources (website organic, paid ads, referrals). A healthy local SEO strategy should show GBP calls growing month over month.</p>
