<h3>Suspension Recovery Process</h3>
<p>If your profile is suspended, follow this exact process:</p>
<p><strong>Phase 1 — Immediate actions (first 24 hours):</strong><br />
- Do NOT create a new profile. This triggers a duplicate listing violation and makes recovery significantly harder.<br />
- Document everything: screenshots, emails, suspension date<br />
- Check your GBP dashboard and email for any specific reason given</p>
<p><strong>Phase 2 — Identify and fix violations (days 1-3):</strong><br />
- Audit your profile against Google's guidelines<br />
- Verify business name matches exactly with your business license<br />
- Confirm address validity and consistency<br />
- Remove any keyword stuffing or promotional language<br />
- Check for duplicate listings and merge or remove them<br />
- Ensure website URL works and matches your business</p>
<p><strong>Phase 3 — Gather documentation:</strong><br />
- Business license or registration certificate<br />
- Utility bill showing business name and address<br />
- Photos of permanent storefront signage (if applicable)<br />
- Lease agreement or property ownership proof<br />
- Professional liability insurance<br />
- Business cards with matching NAP<br />
- Website screenshots showing consistent information</p>
<p><strong>Phase 4 — Submit reinstatement request:</strong><br />
1. Go to Google Business Profile Help Center<br />
2. Use the official appeals/reinstatement tool<br />
3. Fill out the form completely and honestly<br />
4. Upload documentation within the 60-minute window after initiating the appeal<br />
5. Write a concise, factual appeal acknowledging the guidelines, stating violations found and corrected, and referencing attached documentation</p>
<p><strong>Phase 5 — Follow-up:</strong><br />
- Response time: typically 3-14 days, complex cases up to 4-8 weeks<br />
- Check email daily including spam folder<br />
- If no response in 14 days, escalate via the Google Business Profile Help Community forum<br />
- If denied, submit additional review with more documentation</p>
