<h3>Schema Markup Connection</h3>
<p>Connect your GBP to your website using LocalBusiness schema markup. This reinforces your entity relationship with Google and improves your chances of appearing in rich results.</p>
<p><strong>Required schema properties:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><code>@type</code>: LocalBusiness (or specific subtype like <code>Plumber</code>, <code>HVACBusiness</code>, <code>Electrician</code>)</li>
<li><code>name</code>: Exact business name matching GBP</li>
<li><code>address</code>: Physical address (can match hidden GBP address)</li>
<li><code>telephone</code>: Matching phone number</li>
<li><code>url</code>: Location-specific landing page</li>
<li><code>geo</code>: Latitude and longitude coordinates</li>
<li><code>openingHoursSpecification</code>: Business hours</li>
<li><code>priceRange</code>: Price indicator ($, $$, $$$)</li>
<li><code>aggregateRating</code>: Review count and average rating</li>
</ul>
<p>Add this schema to the <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> of your location-specific landing page and validate it using Google's Rich Results Test.</p>
<h3>Voice Search Optimization</h3>
<p>Voice searches are conversational and question-based. Optimize for them by:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Using natural language in your description:</strong> Write how people speak, not how they type</li>
<li><strong>Creating FAQ content:</strong> Answer "who," "what," "where," "when," "why," and "how" questions on your website</li>
<li><strong>Including long-tail keywords:</strong> "Who is the best emergency plumber in Dallas open right now?"</li>
<li><strong>Optimizing for "near me":</strong> Ensure your service areas and location pages are comprehensive</li>
</ol>
<p>Voice search results often pull from featured snippets and AI Overviews. Structure your website content with clear H2 questions and concise 40-60 word answers to increase your chances of being the spoken result.</p>
