<h2>Chapter 9: Your 30-Day GBP Optimization Plan</h2>
<h3>Week 1: Setup and Foundation</h3>
<p><strong>Day 1 — Audit:</strong><br />
- Claim or verify your GBP<br />
- Confirm business name matches legal registration<br />
- Hide your address if you are a service-area business<br />
- Configure service areas (up to 20, within realistic drive time)</p>
<p><strong>Day 2 — Categories:</strong><br />
- Select primary category using the trade-specific recommendations in Chapter 1<br />
- Add 2-4 relevant secondary categories<br />
- Align categories with your website title tags</p>
<p><strong>Day 3 — Core Information:</strong><br />
- Write or rewrite your 750-character business description<br />
- Set accurate business hours including holiday schedules<br />
- Add all relevant attributes (onsite services, free estimates, 24/7, etc.)<br />
- Verify phone number is local and consistent across all platforms</p>
<p><strong>Day 4 — Website Integration:</strong><br />
- Link GBP to a location-specific landing page<br />
- Add UTM parameters for tracking<br />
- Add appointment/booking link if available<br />
- Ensure NAP on your website matches GBP exactly</p>
<p><strong>Day 5 — Services and Products:</strong><br />
- Add every individual service you offer with descriptions<br />
- Include starting prices where possible<br />
- Add product listings if applicable</p>
<p><strong>Day 6 — NAP Consistency Check:</strong><br />
- Audit Yelp, Bing Places, Apple Maps, Facebook, BBB, and industry directories<br />
- Update any inconsistent name, phone, or address information<br />
- Use a tool like Moz Local, BrightLocal, or Yext for bulk auditing</p>
<p><strong>Day 7 — Review and Adjust:</strong><br />
- Check profile completeness using Google's "Profile Strength" indicator<br />
- Fix any missing fields<br />
- Take screenshots of your current profile for before/after comparison</p>
<h3>Week 2: Content and Photos</h3>
<p><strong>Day 8 — Photo Audit:</strong><br />
- Count current photos. If under 20, you need more.<br />
- Remove stock photos, blurry images, and outdated content</p>
<p><strong>Day 9 — Photo Shoot:</strong><br />
- Take 10-15 new photos: team in uniforms, branded vehicles, equipment, job sites<br />
- Capture before/after pairs from a recent project</p>
<p><strong>Day 10 — Photo Optimization:</strong><br />
- Geotag all new photos with your business coordinates<br />
- Rename files with descriptive, keyword-rich names<br />
- Compress to under 200KB each</p>
<p><strong>Day 11 — Photo Upload:</strong><br />
- Upload 5 optimized photos to GBP<br />
- Add captions where possible</p>
<p><strong>Day 12 — First Google Post:</strong><br />
- Create an "Update" post featuring a recent project<br />
- Include a call-to-action button</p>
<p><strong>Day 13 — Offer Post:</strong><br />
- Create an "Offer" post with a seasonal special or new customer discount<br />
- Set an expiration date to create urgency</p>
<p><strong>Day 14 — Website Content:</strong><br />
- Create or update your location-specific landing page<br />
- Add LocalBusiness schema markup<br />
- Publish an FAQ page addressing common customer questions</p>
<h3>Week 3: Reviews and Posts</h3>
<p><strong>Day 15 — Review System Setup:</strong><br />
- Create a direct Google review link using Google's PlaceID tool<br />
- Add the link to your website, email signature, and invoice template<br />
- Set up automated review requests in your CRM or scheduling software</p>
<p><strong>Day 16 — In-Person Training:</strong><br />
- Train technicians to ask for reviews at job completion<br />
- Role-play the in-person ask script from Chapter 5<br />
- Provide each technician with a business card containing the review link QR code</p>
<p><strong>Day 17 — First Review Push:</strong><br />
- Text review requests to 10 recent satisfied customers<br />
- Personalize each message with the specific service performed</p>
<p><strong>Day 18 — Respond to Existing Reviews:</strong><br />
- Respond to every unanswered review on your profile<br />
- Use the templates from Chapter 5</p>
<p><strong>Day 19 — Post Schedule:</strong><br />
- Create a 4-week post calendar using the seasonal calendar from Chapter 4<br />
- Draft posts for the next two weeks</p>
<p><strong>Day 20 — Second Review Push:</strong><br />
- Email review requests to customers from the past 30 days who have not responded to text</p>
<p><strong>Day 21 — Mid-Month Analytics Check:</strong><br />
- Export GBP Performance data<br />
- Note baseline metrics: views, clicks, calls, photo views</p>
<h3>Week 4: Monitoring and Optimization</h3>
<p><strong>Day 22 — Competitor Analysis:</strong><br />
- Check top 3 competitors for your primary keyword<br />
- Compare their review count, photo count, post frequency, and categories<br />
- Identify gaps you can exploit</p>
<p><strong>Day 23 — Q&amp;A Optimization:</strong><br />
- Review existing Q&amp;A on your profile (if available)<br />
- Update your website FAQ page with any new questions you have encountered<br />
- Ensure your description and services cover common customer questions</p>
<p><strong>Day 24 — Photo Upload (Batch 2):</strong><br />
- Upload 5 more optimized photos<br />
- Include at least one before/after pair</p>
<p><strong>Day 25 — Post (Update):</strong><br />
- Publish a project spotlight post with photos</p>
<p><strong>Day 26 — Review Response Round:</strong><br />
- Respond to any new reviews from the past week<br />
- Check competitor reviews for customer complaints you can address in your messaging</p>
<p><strong>Day 27 — Citation Audit:</strong><br />
- Check top 10 directories for NAP consistency<br />
- Fix any discrepancies</p>
<p><strong>Day 28 — Analytics Review:</strong><br />
- Compare Week 4 metrics to Week 1 baseline<br />
- Calculate improvement in views, clicks, and calls<br />
- Identify which posts and photos generated the most engagement</p>
<p><strong>Day 29 — Plan Next Month:</strong><br />
- Set specific targets for reviews, posts, and photos<br />
- Schedule content creation time<br />
- Assign responsibilities to team members</p>
<p><strong>Day 30 — Celebrate and Document:</strong><br />
- Take after screenshots of your profile<br />
- Document improvements in a spreadsheet<br />
- Share wins with your team</p>
